WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.691
- I have a TV show!

00:00:01.691 --> 00:00:02.524
- I know!

00:00:02.524 --> 00:00:03.357
- And you're on it!

00:00:03.357 --> 00:00:04.990
- It's insane actually.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.823
- It's so crazy.

00:00:05.823 --> 00:00:06.680
I am so excited to see,

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:07.930
we never get to see each other really

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.070
'cause we both work so hard but,

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.700
our kids are really close friends,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.540
they always wonder where Dash
and Dylan are and I'm like,

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.760
they're in a different state.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.090
- It's amazing because
my kids have no reference

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.685
for the fact that she is so famous,

00:00:20.685 --> 00:00:21.940
- They think I'm River's mom.
- And so they,

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.560
they think River's mom,
that's who Kelly is

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.680
and when we were doing
Songland on the lot here,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.776
there's pictures of you everywhere

00:00:28.776 --> 00:00:29.609
(laughing)

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:31.710
and our kids would just be
like, oh, there's River's mom.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.750
Why is River's mom's picture everywhere

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.206
and where is yours?

00:00:35.206 --> 00:00:36.486
- [Kelly] And where is yours? (laughing)

00:00:36.486 --> 00:00:37.319
That's so your kids!
- Yeah,

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:38.744
and I was wondering the same thing.

00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:40.330
(laughing)

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.810
- Are you musical at all?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.920
- I was the one white
person, of two white people

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.718
in a black gospel musical on Broadway.

00:00:47.718 --> 00:00:49.151
- Woa.
- So, that means yes.

00:00:49.151 --> 00:00:50.170
- How did that happen?
- I do sing a little bit

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.340
but I didn't have a gospel song

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.150
for my audition so I sang
"Suddenly Seymour" from

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.550
Little Shop of Horrors,
I still got the job.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.220
- I love that song.
- That's amazing.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.440
Here's another thing that's amazing,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.530
you're always up for, I love that my crew

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.020
who was researching you,
like he's up for an award,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.340
I'm like he's always up for awards.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.835
- I love trophies.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.380
(exuberant laughing)

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.795
I'm sorry,

00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:12.628
- That is so Texas.

00:01:12.628 --> 00:01:14.450
- When people call this stuff,

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.510
it is so Texas.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.800
- I actually don't care, man.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.660
- And I know you really don't.
- I know.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.310
- And people will say like, you know,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.900
it's nice to be nominated.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.370
I'm like, give me the trophy.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.410
(loud laughing)

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.920
If you really don't care,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.250
if it really doesn't matter to you,

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.560
if it's just good to be
nominated, I'll take it.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.460
(laughing)

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.088
- I will take that burden for you.

00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:34.921
- Right.

00:01:34.921 --> 00:01:36.360
- No but you are, is it song
of the year for the CMA's?

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.260
- Yes.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:38.728
- You tied a record too?

00:01:38.728 --> 00:01:39.561
- Yes.

00:01:39.561 --> 00:01:41.414
(loud cheering and applause)

00:01:41.414 --> 00:01:42.972
Thank you.
- [Kelly] Is it Rainbow?

00:01:42.972 --> 00:01:45.560
- It's for Rainbow, for Kasey
Musgrave's and actually,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.350
one of my heroes, Alan
Jackson, held the record

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.660
for most nominations for song of the year

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.980
and I just tied that record.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.320
Seven songs in seven years.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.920
(loud cheering and applause)

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.587
- That's so incredible.

00:01:56.587 --> 00:01:59.990
- I am just like, try not to
diminish those kind of things

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.039
like not do the whole, you know,

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.660
when we're given compliments
or when people say,

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.960
god, this is amazing,
we're so drawn to go,

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.020
oh you know, well we'll see.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.490
I mean, how did that happen?

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.070
I'm trying to say you
know what, it is amazing.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:18.070
I am so blessed and so
truly honored to get to do

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.297
what I love and I know
how unusual that is.

00:02:21.297 --> 00:02:23.130
- And how hard you had to work to get it.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.270
- That's exactly right so I do,

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:27.079
I just try to go thank
you, I am a bad ass.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.480
(laughing)
- And I know your story, yes,

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.720
and I do, I know your story
for all of those people

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.900
out there thinking that oh my gosh,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.920
it's never gonna happen,
it's never gonna happen,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.770
it will happen.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.840
You stick with it, dude you
were like living in your car,

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.940
I feel like at one point in (mumbles),

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.218
you were doing like odd jobs.

00:02:42.218 --> 00:02:43.510
- I was sleeping on my sister's couch.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.780
I had been in Nashville at
that point for 14 years,

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.040
trying to get a song
recorded and in and out,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.590
I moved out here for a while.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.540
Actually, when Kelly won American Idol,

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.400
I had friends that knew her
and I became so obsessed

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.440
with if I could just meet Kelly Clarkson,

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.970
I could give her a song.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.320
And it would always happen
where they would always

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.190
hang out without me, and
it wasn't intentional,

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.090
but then I was positive it was.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.710
(laughing)

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.060
- Like, keep him away from her.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.410
- I was so certain that they were like,

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.910
do not bring him around Kelly.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.430
And maybe they were, I mean, I don't know

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.263
but the truth is--

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.778
- No they weren't, they
were all raving about you

00:03:18.778 --> 00:03:19.611
and you kept trying to get--

00:03:19.611 --> 00:03:21.470
- Then you came to a
show where we had to sit,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.858
you had to sit in little kid chairs.

00:03:22.858 --> 00:03:24.425
- In Dallas, yeah.
- In Dallas

00:03:24.425 --> 00:03:25.290
It was like a library.
- I was so excited,

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.780
you were so magical.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.070
You're so great at what you do.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:28.903
- Thank you.

00:03:28.903 --> 00:03:29.736
- You are such a great storyteller,

00:03:29.736 --> 00:03:31.479
which is why have over 40 number one's.

00:03:31.479 --> 00:03:32.312
(loud clapping and cheering)

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.447
- I need these people
with me, all the time.

00:03:33.447 --> 00:03:34.327
- [Kelly] I know.

00:03:34.327 --> 00:03:36.740
- I'm sure doing sitcoms and
having a crowd like respond

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:37.573
to you that way,

00:03:37.573 --> 00:03:39.620
- Yeah, it is wonderful, yeah.
- Wow, yeah.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.040
- They do in my head,
even if they're not here.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:41.960
- [Shane] Me too.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:42.793
(laughing)

00:03:42.793 --> 00:03:44.300
- Like when people don't like what I said,

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.279
just filter it, that was
amazing and so prolific.

00:03:46.279 --> 00:03:47.770
(laughing)

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.020
So let's talk about Songland though,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.280
because I remember when
this idea first came up,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.730
the executive producer Audrey
was telling me about it,

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.670
and I thought god, this is
so genius, the whole idea

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.160
but for everybody that
doesn't know the concept

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.790
of Songland and didn't see it,

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:58.860
tell them what the concept is.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.890
- Yeah, so we have an artist every week,

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.480
and unknown songwriters
are given the opportunity

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.680
to pitch songs to these
artists and it sounded,

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.830
in concept, like yeah,
that's an amazing idea

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.070
but who really wants to watch the process

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.629
that we all do behind the scenes?

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:16.462
- I do.

00:04:16.462 --> 00:04:17.700
- Well, the truth is, it's been amazing

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.480
that people really want to see,

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.463
how did that song get to John Legend?

00:04:22.392 --> 00:04:23.860
- And songs get there
in all different ways.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.660
- Absolutely and sometimes
they go, I like that song

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.000
but it wouldn't work
for me because of this,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.360
so you have the opportunity
right then to change it

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.250
for Macklemore and go, you know what?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.640
Now that there's room for
that, how about try this?

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:39.473
- So cool.

00:04:39.473 --> 00:04:43.300
- It really is like, it's a big leap.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.310
You know, of all those
years you talked about me,

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.290
trying to make it in
songwriting, I thought

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.180
if I can get in the room
with Kelly Clarkson,

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.590
what's happening is these people,

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.423
- Are getting in the room with people.

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:52.390
- They're getting in the room with people

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.172
and so, it's really just
getting to see the process.

00:04:54.172 --> 00:04:55.300
- And you're paying it forward.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.551
- Yeah.
- You're so perfect for it.

00:04:56.551 --> 00:04:57.384
(audience clapping)

00:04:57.384 --> 00:04:58.250
Perfect.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.676
Hilarious, talented.
- I love it.

